## Core Innovations

### 1. Differential Attention
Eliminates background activation noise and prevents head redundancy by computing attention as the difference between two softmax distributions:
$$\text{DiffAttn}(Q, K, V) = \left( \text{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q_1 K_1^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}\right) - \lambda \cdot \text{Softmax}\left(\frac{Q_2 K_2^T}{\sqrt{d_k}}\right) \right) V$$
where $\lambda$ is a learnable scalar initialized to $\lambda = 0.8$.

### 2. Granular Sparse Mixture-of-Experts
Each layer contains 1 shared expert and 4 fine-grained routed experts:
$$y_{FFN} = \text{Expert}_{shared}(x) + \sum_{i \in \text{Top-2}} G(x)_i \cdot \text{Expert}_i(x)$$
$$G(x) = \text{Softmax}(\text{Top-2}(x \cdot W_{gate}))$$
With auxiliary load balancing regularizer:
$$L_{MoE} = N \sum_{i=1}^N f_i \cdot P_i$$

### 3. Compound Multi-Task Loss Objective
$$L_{Total} = L_{CLM} + 0.25 L_{FIM} + 0.01 L_{MoE} + 0.005 L_{Diff}$$
- $L_{CLM}$: Causal next-token prediction
- $L_{FIM}$: Fill-In-The-Middle code & structural infilling (PSM / SPM)
- $L_{MoE}$: Expert routing balance
- $L_{Diff}$: Attention map decorrelation

### 4. Muon 2D Polar Orthogonalization Optimizer
All 2D projection matrices are updated via 5-step Newton-Schulz orthogonalization:
$$M_t = \mu M_{t-1} + \nabla L(W_{t-1})$$
$$O_t = \text{NewtonSchulz}(M_t)$$
$$W_t = W_{t-1} - \eta_t \left( 0.2 \cdot \frac{O_t}{\text{RMS}(O_t)} + \lambda_{wd} W_{t-1} \right)$$
Combined with AdamW for 1D vectors and SSM parameters under a **Warmup-Stable-Decay (WSD)** $(1 - \sqrt{t})$ schedule.

### 5. Native Agentic Control Tokens
- `<|thought start|>` ... `<|thought end|>`: Internal chain-of-thought reasoning
- `<|call tool|>`: Deterministic tool execution trigger
- `<|tool response|>`: Input/API payload reception
- `<|reflect|>`: Error self-correction loop

